<title>UK: West Brom soccer club names Harford manager.</title>
<headline>West Brom soccer club names Harford manager.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>English first division soccer club West Bromwich Albion said on Thursday it had named Ray Harford as team manager, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The club, now listed on London's AIM market as West Bromwich Albion Plc, sacked Alan Buckley late last month, saying it planned to hire a high-profile manager.</p>
<p>Harford previously held management positions at Blackburn Rovers, Wimbledon, Fulham and Luton Town.</p>
